{#
  The recipe view (FSD §8.2, §9) — one to three recipes side by side as a
  cooking sheet, with ingredients and directions.

  **Three columns of 773 px, and the width is fixed even when only one recipe is
  up.** Spreading a single recipe across the full 2400 px would give lines of
  ~160 characters (FSD §7) — measured as unreadable at cooking distance long
  before the type size becomes the problem. So the columns keep their width and
  the row is centred instead.

  Type size comes in per column (``column.font_px``): 28 → 26 → 24 px, decided in
  ``recipe_layout.py`` so one long recipe does not shrink the short ones beside
  it. Nothing here computes it — the template only sets what it is told, which
  is what keeps the rule testable without Chromium.

  Layout follows FSD §7: no line thinner than 3 px, no gradient, no grey below
  170. Black on white, because both are Spectra primaries and carry no dither
  raster at all. ``pre-wrap`` throughout: ``ingredients`` and ``directions`` are
  multi-line free text at Paprika [belegt], not structured lists.
#}<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ language }}">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <title>ePaperEngine</title>
    <style>
      html,
      body {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        width: 2560px;
        height: 1440px;
        overflow: hidden;
        background: #fff;
        color: #000;
        font-family: "DejaVu Sans", sans-serif;
      }
      main {
        box-sizing: border-box;
        width: 2560px;
        height: 1440px;
        padding: 80px;
        display: flex;
        gap: 40px;
        justify-content: center;
        align-items: stretch;
      }
      .column {
        width: 773px;
        flex: none;
        overflow: hidden;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
      }
      /* The 3 px FSD §7 asks for — 1 px disappears on this panel. */
      .column + .column {
        border-left: 3px solid #000;
        padding-left: 37px;
      }
      .title {
        font-weight: bold;
        line-height: 1.1;
        margin-bottom: 12px;
      }
      .meta {
        /* 200 is the grey the panel renders reliably; 170 is the floor. */
        color: #646464;
        margin-bottom: 24px;
      }
      .heading {
        font-weight: bold;
        border-bottom: 3px solid #000;
        padding-bottom: 6px;
        margin: 24px 0 12px;
      }
      .body {
        white-space: pre-wrap;
        line-height: 1.35;
      }
      .cut {
        margin-top: 20px;
        color: #dc1e1e;
        font-weight: bold;
      }
      .empty {
        margin: auto;
        font-size: 56px;
        text-align: center;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      {% if not columns %}
        {# Reachable by pinning the recipe view with nothing selected. A legible
           sentence beats an empty white wall, and beats a failure — nothing is
           broken, there is simply nothing to cook. #}
        <div class="empty">{{ t("recipes.empty") }}</div>
      {% endif %}
      {% for column in columns %}
        <div class="column" style="font-size: {{ column.font_px }}px">
          <div class="title" style="font-size: {{ column.font_px + 16 }}px">{{ column.name }}</div>
          {% if column.meta %}<div class="meta">{{ column.meta }}</div>{% endif %}
          {% if column.ingredients %}
            <div class="heading">{{ t("recipes.ingredients") }}</div>
            <div class="body">{{ column.ingredients }}</div>
          {% endif %}
          {% if column.directions %}
            <div class="heading">{{ t("recipes.directions") }}</div>
            <div class="body">{{ column.directions }}</div>
          {% endif %}
          {% if column.truncated %}
            <div class="cut">{{ t("recipes.truncated") }}</div>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
